CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ dsize of a non-POD class: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ dsize of a POD class: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static assertion failed
could not be evaluated
--
Clang's `__datasizeof(T)' is the Itanium C++ ABI's dsize(T) (ABI 2.2: "the
size of O without tail padding"; 2.4-II: a POD for the purpose of layout has
dsize == sizeof, otherwise dsize is the end of the last non-static data
member, 0 for an empty class; non-class types: sizeof, N5008 [expr.sizeof]).
libc++ 18 preprocessed by clang defines `__libcpp_datasizeof<_Tp>::value =
__datasizeof(_Tp)' and sizes every basic_string copy (`__constexpr_memmove')
with it; the unknown builtin left the value unresolved, so
`std::string("abc")[1]' read nondet under libc++.  The static_asserts were
checked against clang++-18 (g++ 13 does not have the builtin).  Fixed in
round 163b.
